(d) “license” and “licensee” have the same meaning as in the Easements Act, 1882 (V of 1882), and, for the purpose of section 4, “licensee” includes all persons inducted by him into the building to which the license relates;
(e) “unauthorized occupant” means a person who is in occupation of any land or building without the express permission or authority of the Federal Government, and includes___
(i) a person inducted into any land or building by the lessee or licensee thereof; and
(ii) every member of the lessee’s or licensee’s family who remains in occupation of any land or building after the determination of the lease or license in respect of the same.
